implementationPlan.description:
Preconditions and inventory (read-only).

(a) Confirm that every dependsOn row is DONE or ARCHIVED and has landed: `git log --oneline --grep <task id>` on moe/work-2026-10-24 must show its completion commit (feat/fix, not only wip). Confirm that VSC-0 (task-a3e414a3, not in dependsOn) is DONE and that docs/plans/2026-11-02-vscode-reuse.md is on the branch. A DONE row that has not landed is a blocker: call moe.report_blocked naming it instead of gating a partial epic.

(b) Build the per-row table that step 6 needs: label, task id, final status, and landing commit. The landing commit is the short sha of the completion commit: landing.lastCompletion.sha from moe.get_context epicSiblings, cross-checked with git log.

(c) List the epic rows that are NOT in this row's dependsOn:
- VSC-0;
- this row;
- VSC-22, task-be543ff20bbc4f30ac7ac895ae0b4d13 (the JetBrains ChatPanel dead-selection follow-up filed by VSC-6's architect; mem:gotcha-jetbrains-chatpanel-dead-selection);
- any other row filed during the epic (moe.list_tasks epicId epic-aabc654d).

(d) Collect the parked items. Read each row's completionSummary and reviewSummary, with moe.get_context per row or a read-only node read of .moe/tasks/<id>.json. List every note that says out of scope, follow-up, parked, deferred or not pinned. Known now:
- VSC-1 left its docs to this row;
- VSC-3 noted that MoeJson drops exit codes outside the Int range;
- VSC-6 noted that VS Code pushes CHANNEL_CREATED without an id dedupe (JetBrains dedupes).

Error handling: if a moe tool call fails, retry once, then fall back to reading .moe/tasks/*.json read-only. Never edit .moe by hand.

Adversarial pass over the whole epic diff (DoD 5).

First list `git log --format='%h %s' 882a4c39..HEAD -- moe-vscode moe-jetbrains scripts/bundle-manifest.json .github/workflows/ci.yml`. Mark every commit whose subject names no epic task id, so its hunks are not blamed on the epic. Then read `git diff 882a4c39..HEAD` over the same paths. Check at least:
(1) contract drift between a corpus and its consumer, and label drift from MoeBundle.properties;
(2) duplicated helpers, such as a second copy of account text (the VSC-13 port vs the Accounts view) or of shell quoting (the VSC-15 sign-in terminal vs util/AgentLauncher.ts);
(3) strict vm-harness require maps broken by a new import, which shows as a whole test file failing or a test total that dropped;
(4) listeners, terminals, tree providers and timers that are never disposed (the VSC-1 notifier, the VSC-14/15 view, VSC-20/21 seat tracking and onDidCloseTerminal);
(5) notifications fired from STATE_SNAPSHOT or before the first snapshot;
(6) seat deregistration parity: seat ids persisted until WORKER_DEREGISTERED acks them, resent at every connect, and seats the extension did not launch never touched;
(7) webview text built from daemon strings is escaped, the CSP is intact, and there are no new markup-string writes;
(8) Windows and POSIX paths and quoting in every new terminal command;
(9) the bundle manifest read by both builds with no hand-kept second list, and the CI job packaging and smoke-testing the vsix;
(10) the parked items from step 1(d).

For each finding:
- Fix it in this task only if the fix stays inside this task's four doc files.
- Otherwise file a row with moe.create_task in epic-aabc654d: status BACKLOG, title prefixed [VSC-n], a DoD that includes a test. Record its id.

Error handling: when a finding's evidence is ambiguous, write the open question into the filed row instead of guessing a fix.

Update moe-vscode/README.md with the Edit tool. Describe what actually landed: read each row's completionSummary and the code at HEAD, not the plans.

Features, one line each and only for behaviour that shipped:
- task-status notifications with View Task;
- per-task worktrees kept out of file watching and search;
- the Delivery section in task detail;
- blocker parity on the board and in task detail;
- Release Agent;
- the Accounts view and its actions;
- settings parity: enableAgentTeams, the read-only effective landing policy, and the dead branch/commit fields gone;
- seat deregistration when an agent terminal closes;
- deleted chat channels leaving the chat view.

Regenerate the Commands list and the Extension settings table from moe-vscode/package.json (contributes.commands and contributes.configuration at HEAD), so every title and key matches. Under Release notes, add a short Unreleased block that mirrors the CHANGELOG entry. Keep the README's tone and length; no marketing.

Error handling: leave out any feature whose row did not ship (ARCHIVED or scoped down). Never describe one from its plan.

CHANGELOG and manual checks.

moe-vscode/CHANGELOG.md: add one '## [Unreleased]' entry for the epic, above [0.8.0], with Keep a Changelog Added/Changed/Fixed sections. Do not bump the version; versions are synced at release.

moe-vscode/MANUAL_TESTS.md: replace the stale first line. An automated node:test suite now exists (`npm test`), and the manual checks cover what node:test cannot. Add sections in the file's existing style (numbered steps plus Expected lines):
- task notifications: AWAITING_APPROVAL, BLOCKED, REVIEW and DONE; View Task opens the task; no notice on a reconnect snapshot;
- the Accounts view and its sign-in terminal;
- worktree exclusion: a file under .worktrees/ is absent from search and quick open but still listed in the Explorer;
- Release Agent;
- seat deregistration: launch a seat, close its terminal, and the worker deregisters and its task is released;
- a deleted chat channel leaves both the channel list and the selection;
- Remote-WSL, VS Code's answer to JetBrains' 'Run Agents in WSL' toggle: open the project through VS Code Remote-WSL; the extension host and the bundled daemon run inside the distro, and agents launch through moe-agent.sh.

Error handling: leave out the manual check for any behaviour that did not ship.

Final self-review and summary.
(1) DoD 6: `git status --short` and this task's diff touch only moe-vscode/README.md, moe-vscode/CHANGELOG.md, moe-vscode/MANUAL_TESTS.md and docs/plans/2026-11-02-vscode-reuse.md, and none of the description's not-in-scope files. Other sessions' dirty paths are not yours.
(2) Re-read the four docs against HEAD: every command, setting key, behaviour and sha they name exists.
(3) Assemble the summary:
- the Gate A and Gate B commands, exit codes and counts against the baselines;
- the corpus grep listing from step 2;
- every adversarial finding, marked 'fixed here' or given its filed row id;
- each parked item from step 1(d) and what happened to it.
(4) Remove /mnt/d/moe-scratch/vsc18-gate after recording the results.

Error handling: if the re-read finds a doc claim that does not hold, fix the doc and rerun Gate A, because README.md and CHANGELOG.md ship inside the vsix.
